// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2813124391" "Vanguard and the IDF are working on getting the sonic fences up as we speak, {HeroName}. The Vanguard have been fighting off the occasional attack by the Devouring Earth. Serpent Drummer is concerned, though, that the Hamidon is merely toying with us, making us think that we have the upperhand.<br><br>I hope he's wrong, but... well... the guy is usually <i>right</i>. I'm starting to have my doubts about how good of an idea this was, especially with this latest order handed down directly from Lady Grey.<br><br>She says that if the situation gets to a point where the civilization is going to fall, then I need to <color red>shut off the portal to Praetoria. Anyone left there will be considered KIA.</color> Pretty bad, right? I mean, why do I have to do that? I was never up for this! Things were so much simpler when I was just <color yellow>Executable Number 6</color> on the tech sphere and helping out that woman in the computer...<br><br><color orange>{Hero.type=villain You ignore the ramblings of Number Six. The sonic fences should be up and running soon. The Hamidon, however, can still make an attack. The Vanguard seem to think you're still doing this for altruistic reasons, which is quite good for you. They'll never know what's coming until it's too late.}"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Hamidon 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page KilledReese Text :
"P4282552764" "Hello, {HeroName}. I believe it's time you and I talk. I am <color yellow>the Hamidon</color>. I have taken this form to interact with you.<br><br>The heart of man is evil, {HeroName}. At its core, humans are creatures who cannot help but descend into sin, into evil, into <i>destruction</i>. I have seen it, I was <i>once</i> like that, until I ascended, became something more.<br><br>You are here now, trying to stop me, trying to stop the Good from remaking the world, from taking it back. You are fully aware of what humanity has done to the planet, to this <i>gift</i> that they have. It is ignored, it is used, it is destroyed... something so massive as this planet, destroyed by something so... <i>finite</i>.<br><br>You are no better, {HeroName}. You killed the man called Reese. You are here to stop me, but yet you are no better than the others. Why do you continue?"
// Answer Text :
"P2415109101" "I continue because there's hope in humanity, Hamidon."
// Answer Text :
"P2306058609" "I still haven't gotten what -I- want, and I won't stop until I do."
// Answer Text :
"P1489594197" "I don't need to explain myself to you, Hamidon."
// Answer Text :
"P1600427856" "I continue in order to serve justice. Reese killed a companion of mine."
// Page Choice1KilledReese Text :
"P954130813" "Justice? There is no justice in this world, {HeroName}, outside of <i>me</i>. There is no justice for your companion with Reese's death. This is why... this is why you humans are so small... so petty.<br><br>You want something you can't have. Reese's death only serves to satisfy your small needs, the same ones that would destroy you and destroy this planet.<br><br>You and all the other humans do not deserve this place, not in the forms you have now."
// Answer Text :
"P778915094" "Are you saying you're some perfect being, Hamidon?"
// Page FinalPageKilledReese Text :
"P707256491" "I am a perfected being, {HeroName}. As I said... I was once like you, a human. But I discovered another world... a way to become more, to become one with the will of the Earth. My own will and the Earth's will are intertwined now.<br><br>I will remake everything, I will remake life on this world, life that will serve <i>me</i>... serve the world, serve the good. For this to happen, all of the old life must either become part of me or die.<br><br>I gave humanity a chance, {HeroName}, and it failed. What you fight is a battle that you cannot win. Even as we speak, my new life has already moved into the last blight on this earth. It will wipe them all out, just as I will wipe you out here and now."
// Answer Text :
"P3579724911" "We'll see about that, Hamidon."
// Page Hero Text :
"P2552064109" "Hello, {HeroName}. I believe it's time you and I talk. I am <color yellow>the Hamidon</color>. I have taken this form to interact with you.<br><br>The heart of man is evil, {HeroName}. At its core, humans are creatures who cannot help but descend into sin, into evil, into <i>destruction</i>. I have seen it, I was <i>once</i> like that, until I ascended, became something more.<br><br>You are here now, trying to stop me, trying to stop the Good from remaking the world, from taking it back. You are fully aware of what humanity has done to the planet, to this <i>gift</i> that they have. It is ignored, it is used, it is destroyed... something so massive as this planet, destroyed by something so... <i>finite</i>.<br><br>You claim to be a hero of the people, but how can you stand to serve such a limited cause? Your actions do nothing but prolong their doom. Why do you continue, {HeroName}, when you stand for something so meaningless?"
// Page HeroChoice1 Text :
"P1897750319" "Hope? In your humanity? There was never any hope, {HeroName}. Even the strongest humans give in to their weaknesses, to their vices. You are all ruled by them. I have seen this in Emperor Cole and all the others who begged for humanity to be given 'one last chance'.<br><br>In my mercy, I gave them one last chance, and they proved me right. When he was given the chance, Marcus Cole gave into his  vice: pride. It was in his pride that he sought control, and through that, he eventually did an evil that was once done onto him; releasing a nuclear bomb on his own beloved city.<br><br>Don't you see how telling that act was? How it shows how self-destructive you all are? But I am different, {HeroName}. Where you all destroy, I create."
// Answer Text :
"P1540000310" "You call this creation? You're killing everyone!"
// Page FinalPageHero Text :
"P1633098555" "I am purging a problem, {HeroName}. I shall try to put it in a way you understand.<br><br>I am removing the criminal so they never have the chance to commit the crime. Humanity as a whole has proven <i>lacking</i>, they do not deserve the Earth, the beauty that I have seen. I must save this beauty, save this Earth. In order to do that, the problem must be removed.<br><br>You will not get in my way, {HeroName}, not any further. You represent humanity's new Cole, the one who says they can be saved. But I will not give you the same mercy I gave Cole. As we speak, my new life is consuming your last diseased humanity.<br><br>You cannot save them, {HeroName}, for you too will be consumed and become part of something greater, something more beautiful than yourself."
// Answer Text :
"P2160179892" "Others have tried, Hamidon. You'll find I'm hard to kill!"
// Page Villain Text :
"P2543868484" "Hello, {HeroName}. I believe it's time you and I talk. I am <color yellow>the Hamidon</color>. I have taken this form to interact with you.<br><br>The heart of man is evil, {HeroName}. At its core, humans are creatures who cannot help but descend into sin, into evil, into <i>destruction</i>. I have seen it, I was <i>once</i> like that, until I ascended, became something more.<br><br>You are here now, trying to stop me, trying to stop the Good from remaking the world, from taking it back. You are fully aware of what humanity has done to the planet, to this <i>gift</i> that they have. It is ignored, it is used, it is destroyed... something so massive as this planet, destroyed by something so... <i>finite</i>.<br><br>You are no better, {HeroName}. You cause chaos and destruction in your wake, for your own selfish causes. Tell me, why do you do all of this?"
// Page VillainChoice1 Text :
"P2480038530" "Gotten what you want? What is it that you desire? Money? Power? Love? Justice?<br><br>Your needs are useless, {HeroName}. You seek something you can never have. Can you ever have enough to stop? This is the problem with you all.<br><br>You all seek to satisfy yourselves, thinking it will be over, but it never is. You seek more and more, draining the essence out of what you seek until you move on. All the while, the Earth suffers, the planet suffers, because of you. Your actions in search of what will satisfy you destroy that which the Earth would give to you.<br><br>And in time... you would do the same to Earth. You would use it for all of its worth, then look for something greater, discard it like a hollow shell. It does not deserve such a fate, {HeroName}."
// Answer Text :
"P497525973" "Do you think you can stop me, Hamidon?"
// Page FinalPageVillain Text :
"P1433661283" "Fool. I do not 'think' anything. I am a higher being, a being of certainty. It was I who gave mercy to Cole, it was I who allowed Praetoria to flourish for as long as it did. If there is something I want, I make it so.<br><br>I am creation, {HeroName}, and you, you are destruction. In the end, I shall always prevail, for my creation is vast and powerful, while your destruction is petty and meaningless.<br><br>You seek to form a new civilization, but you will fail. As we speak, my new life is overwhelming your rotting city, consuming it, making it new. Your new civilization relied too much on you, and now it will be destroyed.<br><br>As for you, {HeroName}, there is only one option for you. I shall make you part of me, bring you into my new life. You shall be consumed and join something greater."
// Answer Text :
"P50691900" "I'd love to see you try, Hamidon."
// Page NoExplain Text :
"P1256942528" "You do not talk as much as Emperor Cole. Interesting.<br><br>Your efforts, however, are meaningless, {HeroName}. As we speak, my new life is consuming the civilization you thought you could preserve. Your immense power is nothing compared to <i>mine</i>, and it never will be able to stand against it.<br><br>I will take the rest of this planet into myself and form a new, perfect world. You, {HeroName}, will become part of that."
// Answer Text :
"P1726854329" "(Fight the Avatar of Hamidon!)"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P903477152" "Sorry, {HeroName}, I sort of went to a weird place there. We need to focus, right? Right! So, here's the deal.<br><br>It's going to take a while to get the sonic fencing back up to snuff. In the meantime, I've managed to locate a <i>huge</i> area underground where the Devouring Earth's forces are located. Not just that, but I even located, get this, an <color red>Avatar of Hamidon</color>! Crazy!<br><br>Were you there when the first Avatar was found? It was terrifying, from what I heard! Luckily for us, that one was actually a bit of an anomaly; it had been there for a <i>very</i> long time.<br><br>Your average Avatar isn't as strong as that... well, we hope. At least, the one I found isn't that bad!"
// AcceptString :
"P496893499" "You're suggesting I destroy this Avatar of Hamidon."
// SendOffString :
"P258157840" "That's it precisely! The Devouring Earth tend to flock around these Avatars. They're leader figures in a sense.<br><br>Plus, well, to be honest, we kind of need to focus Hamidon's attention <i>away</i> from Last Bastion, and the best way to do that is throw a buffed up Incarnate like you <i>straight</i> at one of its prized possessions!<br><br>I'm sorry that I'm asking you to do such a dangerous thing, {HeroName}, but, well, it kind of comes with the territory of fighting to save a civilization from a giant earth monster.<br><br>Just make sure you're prepared, ok? <color orange>The Avatar of Hamidon is no joke, so if you're going to go against it, you need to bring all the firepower you can muster!</color><br><br>In the meantime, I'm going to investigate some odd readings I'm getting from Anti-Matter's space station. I don't know what it could be, but someone turned <i>something</i> on in there. It could be him!"
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1260735890" "Attack an Avatar of Hamidon"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P4254770618" "I'm kind of glad my only super power is to jump into computers. I could never be brave enough to do what <i>you're</i> about to do!"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P3507560543" "<color deepskyblue>Part Four: The New Champion</color>"

